# No hardcoded install prefixes

Do not embed machine-local or package-manager prefixes in C, C++, CMake, or test helpers (`/opt/homebrew`, `/usr/local`, `/opt/local`, `C:\LLVM`, …). If you see one, remove it in the same change.

Discover instead:

- Environment: `VULKAN_SDK`, `HOMEBREW_PREFIX`, `LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX`, `YONA_HOME`, `YONA_PATH`
- Tools: `brew --prefix`, `brew --prefix <formula>`, `pkg-config`, `xcrun --show-sdk-path`
- CMake: `find_path` / `find_library` / `find_package`, then generate a header if the runtime needs the result

```c
/* BAD */
dirs[n++] = "/opt/homebrew/lib";

/* GOOD — env, then CMake-recorded dir, then bare soname */
const char* brew = getenv("HOMEBREW_PREFIX");
```

Docs may mention example prefixes in install instructions. Runtime and build logic must not copy those examples into search lists.

Product FHS roots that packaging actually installs (`/usr/lib/yona`) stay next to the packager, not copied into new features as a catch-all.
